    "abstract": "This is a tutorial on reading and processing RAW photo files with\n     Python. A RAW file stores unprocessed sensor readings. Therefore\n     several conversion steps need to be applied before it can be displayed.\n     Typically these steps are applied by the camera firmware or by a RAW\n     development tool on the PC. In contrast this work presents a program-\n     matic Python/NumPy based workflow allowing to easily modify the\n     individual steps. Each required processing step is motivated and dis-\n     cussed.",
